{"seq":65,"slug":"lock-free-concurrent-data-structures","title":"无锁与并发数据结构","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures","rating":{"composite":3.86,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"无锁与并发数据结构\">无锁与并发数据结构</h1><p>多核已经是十几年前就尘埃落定的现实，但「让多个线程同时安全地读写同一份数据」始终是工程里最容易出错的角落。一把互斥锁能解决正确性，却会把所有线程串成一列，让你昂贵的核心轮流空转；而真正榨干多核吞吐的无锁结构，又要求你直面 CPU 重排、缓存一致性、回收时机这些平时被锁悄悄掩盖的硬骨头。这个 hub 的目的，是带你从「为什么共享内存会骗人」一路走到「如何写出一个能上生产、且不会在某个 0.01% 的时序里崩掉的无锁容器」。</p>\n<p>整个 hub 由四章构成，按依赖顺序层层递进，每一章都是下一章的地基。</p>\n<p>第一章「基础」回答最底层的问题：当两个线程不加协调地访问同一块内存时，到底会发生什么。我们先把竞态、撕裂、可见性这些「危险」讲清楚，再引入硬件与语言共同约定的内存模型与内存序，最后落到所有无锁算法的原子砖块——CAS 与其它读改写原语。没有这一章，后面的一切都是空中楼阁。</p>\n<p>第二章「进展保证」把视角从「会不会出错」抬升到「会不会卡住」。我们对比锁与无锁两种范式的真实代价，给出无等待、无锁、无阻塞三个进展级别的严格定义与判别方法，并专门拆解几乎每个 CAS 算法都绕不开的 ABA 问题。这一章给你的是一套词汇与判据，让你能精确地说出「我这个结构提供什么样的进展保证」。</p>\n<p>第三章「数据结构」是把前两章的理论落到具体容器：从最经典的 Michael-Scott 无锁队列与 Treiber 栈，到工业级并发哈希表的分段与开放寻址之争，再到 Harris-Michael 无锁链表与无锁跳表。每一种结构都有它独特的并发难点与久经考验的解法。</p>\n<p>第四章「内存回收与实践」收口最棘手也最容易被忽视的一环：在无锁结构里，「谁来 free、何时 free」本身就是一个并发问题。我们详解危险指针与 epoch 两大回收方案，剖析 Linux 内核与 C++26 都已采纳的 RCU，最后用一章工程陷阱把全 hub 的知识拉回真实战场——内存序用错、false sharing、benchmark 骗局这些让无人代码翻车的真实坑。</p>\n<p>读完这四章，你不仅能读懂别人的无锁代码，更能判断「这里到底该不该上无锁」，并在该上的时候写得对。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"concurrency-hazards","title":"并发风险：竞态与撕裂","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/foundations/concurrency-hazards"},{"seq":2,"slug":"memory-model-ordering","title":"内存模型与内存序","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/foundations/memory-model-ordering"},{"seq":3,"slug":"atomics-cas","title":"原子操作与 CAS","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/foundations/atomics-cas"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"progress","title":"进展保证","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/progress","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"locking-vs-lockfree","title":"锁与无锁对比","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/progress/locking-vs-lockfree"},{"seq":2,"slug":"progress-guarantees","title":"无等待、无锁与无阻塞","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/progress/progress-guarantees"},{"seq":3,"slug":"aba-problem","title":"ABA 问题","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/progress/aba-problem"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"structures","title":"数据结构","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/structures","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"lock-free-queues-stacks","title":"无锁队列与栈","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/structures/lock-free-queues-stacks"},{"seq":2,"slug":"concurrent-hashmaps","title":"并发哈希表","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/structures/concurrent-hashmaps"},{"seq":3,"slug":"lock-free-lists","title":"无锁链表与跳表","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/structures/lock-free-lists"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"reclamation","title":"内存回收与实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/reclamation","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"memory-reclamation","title":"内存回收：危险指针与 epoch","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/reclamation/memory-reclamation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"rcu","title":"RCU 读拷贝更新","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/reclamation/rcu"},{"seq":3,"slug":"practical-pitfalls","title":"工程实践与陷阱","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/lock-free-concurrent-data-structures/reclamation/practical-pitfalls"}]}]}